      "writtenOn": "2026-01-23T20:11:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current `fBackendLabelDirty` setup is not threadsafe. The issue is that an update to `fBackendLabelDirty` must be visible to other threads only *after* an update to the label. So, accesses need to be upgraded to atomic.  \n\nIf we can guarantee that only a single thread modifies labels at a time (but the updates to the label need to be coherent among threads), then I think acquire/release semantics should be sufficient guarantee correct ordering.\n\nIf there are many potential writers, then a mutex is necessary to prevent clobbering the label.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 275,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 301,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
